{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/378975-conversion-project-help","id":378975,"title":"Conversion Project (Help!)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-01-23T06:45:48-08:00","id":378975,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon9.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Conversion Project (Help!)","content":"Some of you already know this, but I've been going on and off about converting the setting of Warhammer Fantasy into the Storyteller's d10 system (mostly because the current rules of WFRPG are a little over my head to keep track of--but the setting has a lot of potential for fun roleplaying).<br /> <br /> I'm looking for suggestions, and brainstorming ideas on how to further develop the mechanics of the game, specifically races, critters, spells, and rituals. A think tank! A think tank! My kingdom for a think tank!<br /> <br /> Here's a link to the project, still in beta: War Fantasy Project<br /> <br /> Edit: , but here's what I've archived!<br /> <br /> <b>d10 Warhammer Fantasy</b><br /> <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,835.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">Errata -- MP's hall of f*ckups</a><br /> <a href=\"https://web.archive.org/web/20151109203646/http://calloftea.com/forum/index.php?topic=5116.0\" target=\"_blank\">Overview &amp; Character Creation</a><br /> <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,297.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">Races</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://web.archive.org/web/20151109201136/http://calloftea.com/forum/index.php?topic=5087.0\" target=\"_blank\">List of Arcane Lores</a><br /> <a href=\"https://web.archive.org/web/20151109201327/http://calloftea.com/forum/index.php?topic=5108.0\" target=\"_blank\">Familiars Expanded</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://web.archive.org/web/20151109201306/http://calloftea.com/forum/index.php?topic=5106.0\" target=\"_blank\">Mutations</a><br /> <a href=\"https://web.archive.org/web/20151109201238/http://calloftea.com/forum/index.php?topic=5127.0\" target=\"_blank\">Chaos Sorcery</a><br /> <a href=\"https://web.archive.org/web/20151109202333/http://calloftea.com/forum/index.php?topic=5491.0\" target=\"_blank\">Diseases, Toxins &amp; Cure-Alls</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://web.archive.org/web/20151109201209/http://calloftea.com/forum/index.php?topic=5630.0\" target=\"_blank\">Esoteric Arcane Lores</a><br /> <a href=\"https://web.archive.org/web/20151109202318/http://calloftea.com/forum/index.php?topic=5089.0\" target=\"_blank\">Merit List</a><br /> <a href=\"https://web.archive.org/web/20151109204021/http://calloftea.com/forum/index.php?topic=5494.0\" target=\"_blank\">Deities &amp; Sanctified Magic</a><br /> <a href=\"https://web.archive.org/web/20151109204326/http://calloftea.com/forum/index.php?topic=5117.0\" target=\"_blank\">Barracks &amp; Armoury</a><br /> <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,288.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">High Magic &amp; True Dhar</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://web.archive.org/web/20151109202113/http://calloftea.com/forum/index.php?topic=5093.0\" target=\"_blank\">Old World Compacts &amp; Conspiracies</a><br /> <a href=\"https://web.archive.org/web/20151109202137/http://calloftea.com/forum/index.php?topic=5275.0\" target=\"_blank\">Vampirism</a><br /> <a href=\"https://web.archive.org/web/20151109202055/http://calloftea.com/forum/index.php?topic=5111.0\" target=\"_blank\">Ye Olde Bestiary</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":974,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","user":"MrParaduo","date":".  Old link was broken 04-18-2018, 09:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-26T08:20:28-08:00","id":381991,"title":"","content":"Well I'd be happy to a wall to bounce ideas off, but my knowledge of warhammer is limited to having a single warhammer 40k book, so my ability to help you proactively is rather limited.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-26T09:12:37-08:00","id":382056,"title":"","content":"That's totally fine. Just having someone to talk with can be a real help.<br /> So what do you think of the magic system? Is it too complicated? I'm having trouble developing rules for designing rituals and the like. According to the source material, rituals are supposed to be expensive and/or epic--but what if it allows non-magician characters to cast spells from the various Lores, but at a price?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-26T14:03:51-08:00","id":382293,"title":"","content":"I've been trying to figure out how to do WFRP-style casting + corruption for a while, but I hadn't considered having the ST roll for it. That's a really neat idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Before enlightenment: chop wood, carry water. After enlightenment: Glorious Tree-Felling Prana and All-Encompassing Liquid-Carrying Methodology.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1223-dorchadas","name":"Dorchadas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1223_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"76"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-26T15:19:47-08:00","id":382372,"title":"","content":"Thank you! I'm glad I made an impression. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-26T22:29:25-08:00","id":382755,"title":"","content":"All righty, let me take a fresh look.<br /> <br /> Magical backlash is worse if you get an exceptional success, that's kind of anti intuitive in the storytelling system.<br /> <br /> Rank says look at the magician merit, but the magician merit grants magic dots, so I'd suggest replacing rank with magic there. <br /> <br /> That's all that jumped out at me, it doesn't seem too complicated to me. I'd have merged lesser magic and petty magic into one merit, with some spells costing three points and some spells costing only one, but that's more symantics than anything really.<br /> <br /> As for making rituals expensive and epic, that sounds like the ritual magic system from the Mage chroniclers guide, do you have that?<br /> <br /> It has rules for spellcasting requiring time, help, and ingredients, and it even includes the option for muggles to be able to use ritual magic also,<br /> <br /> I don't have the book right in front of me, but it rates things by how many ingredients they need.<br /> <br /> If you want a spell to be epic enough you can have the ingredients include the breath of a fish and the footfalls of a cat or some such, so that getting the ingredients are epic in and of itself unless you're as rich as midas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-27T05:52:45-08:00","id":382990,"title":"","content":"Sounds prudent enough. I'm also having problems with divine magic, in that there are potentially a bugillion gods in the Old World, and each of the human deities has their own Divine Lore. Since this game opens up the variety-pack on playable races, that would mean I have to make all new Lores to put on each god. Do you think I can streamline it somehow?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-27T06:58:00-08:00","id":383037,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrParaduo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/378975-conversion-project-help?p=382372#post382372\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thank you! I'm glad I made an impression. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>After a bit of thought, I did realize that the odds of Tzeentch's Curse are <i>much</i> higher with nWoD probabilities than with the original WFRP ones. A one-dot spell has a 33% chance of a curse, compared with a 0% chance of Magic 1 causing it in WFRP (though there is the 10% chance of insanity, admittedly). A two-dot spell is a 50% chance of at least a minor curse, compared to Magic 2 being a 10% chance in WFRP, and a five-dot spell is over 80% (over 90% with an Exceptional Success)! If you don't want Manifestations coming up all the time, it might be better to make Manifestation rolls only count 10s as successes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Before enlightenment: chop wood, carry water. After enlightenment: Glorious Tree-Felling Prana and All-Encompassing Liquid-Carrying Methodology.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1223-dorchadas","name":"Dorchadas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1223_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"76"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-27T07:48:03-08:00","id":383104,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dorchadas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/378975-conversion-project-help?p=383037#post383037\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> After a bit of thought, I did realize that the odds of Tzeentch's Curse are <i>much</i> higher with nWoD probabilities than with the original WFRP ones. A one-dot spell has a 33% chance of a curse, compared with a 0% chance of Magic 1 causing it in WFRP (though there is the 10% chance of insanity, admittedly). A two-dot spell is a 50% chance of at least a minor curse, compared to Magic 2 being a 10% chance in WFRP, and a five-dot spell is over 80% (over 90% with an Exceptional Success)! If you don't want Manifestations coming up all the time, it might be better to make Manifestation rolls only count 10s as successes.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll admit, you make a valid point. What if we used one's magical rank as a balancing factor? Eg. 5 dot Spell - Magic Rank = Manifestation Dice Pool, with modifiers ranging from +/-5 when appropriate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-27T09:05:27-08:00","id":383185,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrParaduo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/378975-conversion-project-help?p=383104#post383104\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll admit, you make a valid point. What if we used one's magical rank as a balancing factor? Eg. 5 dot Spell - Magic Rank = Manifestation Dice Pool, with modifiers ranging from +/-5 when appropriate.</div> </div> </div> </div>That could work if you treated a result of 0 or less as a Chance Die instead of not needing a roll. Maybe then add a Merit for spells some level below your rank (Rank - 3, maybe?) not needing to roll Manifestation at all unless there's a positive modifier in play.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Before enlightenment: chop wood, carry water. After enlightenment: Glorious Tree-Felling Prana and All-Encompassing Liquid-Carrying Methodology.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1223-dorchadas","name":"Dorchadas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1223_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"76"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-27T10:31:59-08:00","id":383280,"title":"","content":"Excellent. Fixed and done.<br /> Still need to work on Divine Magic, though. Also wonder if I should make mechanics for Skavin mutation-sculpting...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-27T14:20:29-08:00","id":383582,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrParaduo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/378975-conversion-project-help?p=383280#post383280\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Excellent. Fixed and done.<br /> Still need to work on Divine Magic, though. Also wonder if I should make mechanics for Skavin mutation-sculpting...</div> </div> </div> </div>Skaven generally aren't player characters and don't sculpt player characters, so actual rolls to that end might be unnecessary. Might be a useful specialty in Occult, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"lin